-- title:
--   Glued supersingular polar pair from two integral q-expansions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$ (a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra). Let $W$ be an Atkin–Lehner datum for $(M,p)$, i.e. $R$ with $M = pR$ together with integers $a,b$ satisfying $pa - Rb = 1$, and let $e \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ have image $\bar e$ in $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ with $\bar e\,\bar p = 1$. Let $f$ be a weight-$2$ cusp form for $\Gamma_H(M)$, the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained from the preimage of $H$ under the lower-right-entry character $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $f$ lies in the two-cusp integral set for $(M,H,2,p)$ and the subring $\bot \subseteq \mathbb{C}$: for every operator $t$ in the Hecke ring $\mathtt{heckeRingH}\,M\,H\,2$, every Atkin–Lehner datum at $(M,p)$ and every $n$, the $n$-th $q$-coefficients of $t f$ and of $(tf)\mid_2 W'$ are rational integers. Let $pf, pfW \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ be integral $q$-expansions, meaning that their images in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ are the $q$-expansions (of width $1$) of $f$ and of $\mathrm{alSlash}\,W\,2$ applied to the diamond operator $\langle e \rangle f$ respectively. Write $\Gamma' = \Gamma_{H'}(M/p)$ with $H'$ the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and let $F = \mathtt{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,K\,\Gamma'$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ over $K$ generated by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma'$. Let $\omega, \omega' \in \Omega[F/K]$ both be supersingular polar differentials: regular at every place of $F/K$ outside $\mathtt{ssPlacesQExp}\,K\,\Gamma'\,p$ and with at most a simple pole at each place in that set. Assume finally that the $q$-expansion map on differentials, $\mathtt{diffQExp}$, sends $\omega$ to the reduction $\mathtt{intSeriesC}\,K\,pf$ of $pf$ and $\omega'$ to the reduction of $pfW$. Then the pair $(\omega, \omega')$ belongs to $\mathtt{twoCompRegularDifferentials}\,K\,\Gamma'\,p$, the $K$-span of the pairs satisfying $\mathtt{IsGluedPolarPair}$ for the set of supersingular node pairs $\mathtt{ssNodePairsQExp}\,K\,\Gamma'\,p$.
--
--   This is the gluing step of the two-cusp $q$-expansion principle: the two differentials prescribed by the two integral $q$-expansions of a weight-two form at level $M$ with $p \parallel M$ are the restrictions to the two components of the mod-$p$ fibre of a single differential on the semistable curve, which amounts to opposite residues at the supersingular crossings. It is used in the construction of the isomorphism between integral two-cusp cusp forms and regular differentials on the two-component curve, and in the resulting equality of ranks.
